Z||000000||penetrator||08-19-99||08:18 AM||||Hi, my fiero GT 86 V6 Stalls when it has reached the workingtemp when im stops at trafficlights and basicly when im engaging the cluth, the RPM goes down to zero. Is it the IAC that needs to be cleand? I got a lowtemp powertermostat and lowtemp fan switch, Fierostores Sprint headers And i have drilled up the plastic intake barrier on the side of the car, it work OK until about 2 weeks ago, when it started to stall.<p>And i also got a new noise that comes in some RPMs , it seams to come from leftside and i think it is from the gearbox. Some have told me it can be the releasebearing(I changed the clutch disc and releasebearing also). Or is it just some vibrations that are normal in some cars ?<p>Please help<br>
Z||000001||Kage86GT4SP||08-20-99||08:48 AM||||gearbox noise:<p>DOUBLE CHECK your gearbox oil level (which is a pain in the a**, since you have to unbolt the speed sensor - NOT the brightest piece of engineering Pontiac showed on this car)<p>I just got my car not too long ago (2 months) (86SE actually... I didn't know the difference when I picked my name, and also a V6)and hadn't checked the level, just "assuming."  I got off the freeway after a nice, 100 mile jaunt down I-5 from Olympia to Vancouver.<p>At the second stop sign, the gear box started making some wierd noises.  It worked fine, good clutch action, but sounded really strange (fortunately, no grinding).<p>Thinking the worst, I had a friend car-dolly it home (again, fortunately, it could have been, say, Vader where it got wierd on me... and THEN, where would I be?)<p>And when I pulled the sensor, there was NO oil on it... and, as it turned out, I was 2 QUARTS LOW!<p>I filled it up a week ago, and have put 200 miles on it since without any problem...<p>So... check that level out!<p>K.
Z||000002||penetrator||08-24-99||04:17 AM||||Thanks<p>Yes, i have checked the gearbox fluid and its filld with 3 quaters, i also changed the oil, but the sound is still there.<br>I can hear it mostly when i got the 2nd gear in and releaseing the gaspedal, and let the car slow down without braking (Engine braking) and the speed is about 10-15 mph.<br>And i also dropped my speedometer gear in the gearbos when i changed the oil =( <br>But the gearbox noise was there before, thats why i changed the oil =)<p>Thanks<br>Magnus
Z||000003||theogre||08-24-99||12:16 PM||||That's what is called a "coast" noise. It's when the load changes from the drive face of a gear to the back face. the back face wears diferantly from the front wich gets more load more often. If the noise happened more when you were on the pedal it would be a drive noise.<p>If it's only doing this in one gear, it's likely the gears are worn. There's not much in the tranny to adjust. There could be a shim or something that wore out but that's about it. The shifter is functioning so it's not that.<p>With the very deep first gear that's in many Fieros I'm not suprised if second is worn the most. It seems to take allot more abuse than first.
